'''Battle of Timor''' was an engagement of the period.

== Background ==
The armies had been manoeuvring for several days before the engagement, and each commander expected the other to give battle on the ground he had chosen.

The opening moves were cautious. Both sides probed the flanks and sent forward skirmishers, and the main bodies did not come into contact until the afternoon.

By evening the field had been cleared and the losing side withdrew in good order, leaving the victor in possession of the ground.
